\details{
The user inputs for this module are separated from the outputs to allow for
more flexible UI design.

The module draws the sample PCA of a bulk expression experiment, the first
plot of most RNA-seq analyses: the counts of a \code{SummarizedExperiment} are
transformed, the most variable genes kept, and the samples projected onto
their principal components (\code{\link[=sample_pca]{sample_pca()}}). The scores are drawn by the
\code{\link[=pcaBiplotInputsUI]{pcaBiplotInputsUI()}} module, so the component axes (titled with the variance
each explains), the loading arrows and every scatter control apply; those
inputs are documented there. Colour and shape choices come from \code{colData}.

To see the scree, loadings, pairs or PC-metadata correlation views of the
same PCA, build it with \code{\link[=sample_pca]{sample_pca()}} and pass it to \code{\link[=pcaScreePlotServer]{pcaScreePlotServer()}}
and friends.
}
\section{Plot parameters and defaults}{

The following parameters can be accessed via UI inputs and/or the \code{defaults} argument:
\itemize{
\item \code{pca.assay} - Assay (UI: "Assay", default: \code{"counts"} when present)
